    <string name="guide_section_sessions">Recorded sessions</string>
    <string name="guide_holding">Hold the phone upright at chest height, screen towards you, camera pointing across the street. Sweep slowly left and right until the sonar tone speeds up and centres. Keep it still while you read the signal.</string>
    <string name="guide_sound_sonar">Repeating tick that speeds up as the signal moves towards the centre of view, panned to the ear it is on.</string>
    <string name="guide_sound_centered">Short double tick: the signal is straight ahead.</string>
    <string name="guide_sound_walk">Rising chime: the walk sign came on while you were watching.</string>
    <string name="guide_sound_stop">Low tone: don’t walk.</string>
    <string name="guide_sound_alert">Two quick beeps from one ear: a vehicle is approaching from that side.</string>
    <string name="guide_sound_critical">Urgent repeated beeps: a vehicle is close and closing fast.</string>
    <string name="guide_sound_veer">Soft tone in one ear while crossing: you are drifting towards that ear.</string>
    <string name="guide_sound_lost">Falling tone: the signal left the camera view.</string>
    <string name="guide_haptic_walk">Two long pulses: walk.</string>
    <string name="guide_haptic_dont">One long pulse: don’t walk.</string>
    <string name="guide_haptic_flashing">Three short pulses: flashing, the interval is ending.</string>
    <string name="guide_haptic_alert">Sharp double buzz: vehicle warning.</string>
    <string name="guide_haptic_tick">Single tick: the signal is centred.</string>
    <string name="guide_trouble_nosignal">If no signal is found: check the lens is clear, hold the phone upright and sweep slowly. Some crossings have no pedestrian signal at all.</string>
    <string name="guide_trouble_nosound">If you hear nothing: check the phone is not silent, that Speech and Tones are on in Settings, and that any headphones are connected.</string>
    <string name="guide_trouble_slow">If the frame rate is low: close other apps, or turn the preview off in Settings.</string>
    <string name="guide_trouble_model">If the model is missing: import a .tflite in Settings, or reinstall a build with one bundled.</string>
